# What not to upload to Vercel. Both services build from this upload: the site from `web/frontend/`
# and the API container from the root (see `.dockerignore` for what that image takes). So
# `generator/`, `templates/` and `tokens/` must stay; build output inside them must not, or the CLI
# packs gigabytes of Gradle and Xcode output to deliver a few megabytes.

**/build/
**/.gradle/
**/.kotlin/
**/.cxx/
**/.idea/
**/captures/
**/__pycache__/
**/DerivedData/
**/.build/
**/xcuserdata/
**/.swiftpm/
**/kotlin-js-store/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
*.zip

# Local working state that is in .gitignore but not, by itself, kept out of an upload. The agent
# directories are anchored to the root: the templates ship their own `.claude/skills/`, which every
# generated project needs.
/out/
/tools/
/.claude/
/.agents/
.venv/
venv/

# Signing material and anything that has ever held a secret.
**/local.properties
**/keystore.properties
**/keys/
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
